---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Controlled darkness — AXYRO">
  <main class="article-page">
    <section class="article-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">JOURNAL / EARTH PHASE</p>

      <span class="index">03</span>

      <h1>Controlled darkness.</h1>

      <p class="sub">
        Darkness as structure rather than aesthetic.
      </p>
    </section>

    <article class="article-body">
      <p>
        Darkness is often treated as mood.
        AXYRO treats darkness as infrastructure.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most modern interfaces use darkness for visual identity.
        Deep blacks, glow effects and contrast become stylistic language.
      </p>

      <p>
        But controlled darkness is different.
        It reduces pressure instead of increasing stimulation.
      </p>

      <p>
        Darkness should absorb noise,
        soften visual aggression
        and create distance between the user and unnecessary interface tension.
      </p>

      <p>
        In AXYRO, black is never pure decoration.
        It behaves like environmental material:
        soft, layered, atmospheric and restrained.
      </p>

      <p>
        The goal is not cinematic drama.
        The goal is sustained focus over long periods of interaction.
      </p>

      <p>
        A calmer system does not demand attention.
        It quietly supports it.
      </p>
    </article>

    <section class="article-footer">
      <a href="/journal">← Back to journal</a>

      <span>
        AXYRO JOURNAL / 03
      </span>
    </section>
  </main>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .article-page {
    min-height: 100vh;

    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 72% 18%,
        rgba(167,216,255,0.025),
        transparent 36%
      ),
      linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        #020407 0%,
        #030712 100%
      );
  }

  .article-hero {
    padding:
      260px
      clamp(32px, 8vw, 160px)
      120px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 42px;

    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.44em;
    text-transform: uppercase;

    color: rgba(167,216,255,0.68);
  }

  .index {
    display: block;

    margin-bottom: 34px;

    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.38em;

    color: rgba(245,247,250,0.22);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;

    font-size: clamp(72px, 8vw, 132px);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: -0.08em;
    font-weight: 430;

    color: rgba(245,247,250,0.96);
  }

  .sub {
    margin-top: 34px;

    max-width: 620px;

    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.7;

    color: rgba(245,247,250,0.52);
  }

  .article-body {
    max-width: 680px;

    margin-left: clamp(32px, 8vw, 160px);

    padding:
      40px
      0
      120px;
  }

  .article-body p {
    margin: 0 0 38px;

    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.2vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.42;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 360;

    color: rgba(245,247,250,0.82);
  }

  .article-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 32px;

    padding:
      64px
      clamp(32px, 8vw, 160px)
      96px;

    border-top:
      1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
  }

  .article-footer a,
  .article-footer span {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.34em;
    text-transform: uppercase;

    color: rgba(245,247,250,0.32);

    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .article-footer a:hover {
    color: rgba(167,216,255,0.72);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .article-hero {
      padding:
        170px
        24px
        76px;
    }

    .article-body {
      margin-left: 24px;
      margin-right: 24px;
    }

    .article-footer {
      flex-direction: column;

      padding-left: 24px;
      padding-right: 24px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(60px, 16vw, 88px);
    }
  }
</style>